  "releaseNotes": "Online archive mailboxes are reached. The archive's distinguished folders (archivemsgfolderroot, archiveinbox, archivedeleteditems and its Recoverable Items), its folders and items by their ids, FindFolder, FindItem, GetItem, CreateItem, UpdateItem, DeleteItem, attachments, SyncFolderItems, SyncFolderHierarchy and pull subscriptions work as in the mailbox itself. MoveItem and CopyItem go between the mailbox and its archive. ArchiveItem moves items into the archive under the source folder's path, as EWS does; it needs MailboxItem.ImportExport.All. An archive id an application saved is routed to the archive after a restart too. A mailbox without an archive answers as before.",
